WEBVTT

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.280
I'm finally here!

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.490
The royal capital of the Kingdom of Tils!

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.420
The palace is just a little smaller 
than the Kingdom of Brandel's.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.600
Wh-Who are you calling a country girl?

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.670
It's normal the first time you 
go somewhere! Anyone would—

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:42.790
I did it again!

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.580
Yes.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.360
We do have a room available.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.320
It's five silvers a night.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.320
Meals are an additional fee.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.450
Also, one basin of hot water is five coppers.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.830
Oh, I can handle hot and cold water myself,
 so I won't be needing any.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:00.860
There we go.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:01.980
That's amazing!

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:03.620
It's magic, right?

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.530
Oh! Are you a Hunter, Miss?

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.470
You're half right.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:13.010
I've actually been accepted to the 
Hunters' Prep School here in this country.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.200
I'm Mile.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.510
I'll be staying here until 
the school entrance ceremony.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.670
I'm the face of this inn, Lenny!

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.350
Do your best out there, miss!

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:28.160
If a famous Hunter favored our inn, 
we'd start really raking it in!

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.880
I'm not interested in standing out like that.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:30.860
What's this?

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.560
I'm aiming for just one thing!

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:37.570
Absolutely average, completely unremarkable,
 everyday happiness!

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:41.030
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:46.000
<b>You Said I'd Get a Do-Over in a New World!</b>

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.420
Okay! Time for a redo of 
my life in a new world!

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.170
This time I'm going to find normal happiness!

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:55.710
Have a nice day!

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.300
Thank you!

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.350
I'll start by getting a feel for this town.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:04.560
Oh, I want to eat gelato!

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.560
<b>Sapain Square</b>

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.600
<b>Arena</b>

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.600
Wow! What a gorgeous view!

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.400
<b>Dragon's Mouth</b>

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.900
My hand! My hand!

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.730
Oh, dear!

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.280
Just kidding!

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.910
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.830
Now that I'm done sightseeing, 
I'll head for the marketplace.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.790
Oh, I see...

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.380
I thought this town was a little subdued.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:39.800
I haven't really seen
any children besides Lenny-chan.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.050
Could it be that even in this fantasy world,

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.470
they've been hit with declining birth rates?

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.230
Oops. Careful there.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.570
I'm so sorry!

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:58.280
Um, thank you very much.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:03.160
Um... Mister... Miss...

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:04.240
Miss Sir?

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.450
Yes... In trying to be considerate, 
you got a little mixed up.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.170
If you daydream too much and get lost,

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.960
you might not find your way back home.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.170
I-I'm not that little!

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.380
Well then, I'll take my leave.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.600
Oh, and... I'm a woman.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.020
So that bothered her.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:35.360
<i>That aside... Treating me 
like a child was pretty rude.</i>

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.570
<i>Despite my appearance, my actual age is...</i>

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.780
You there, little one.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:40.570
Huh?

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.780
Turn back right now.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.080
A child walking into the 
slums without a care...

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.040
They'd chew you up and suck on your bones.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.500
A child?

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.160
You're littler than me. It's obvious.

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:55.750
At any rate, I'm saying 
to stay away from there.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:00.170
Wow... It's like the perfect depiction 
of a seedy underworld.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:01.800
I'm sorry!

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.680
I was thinking and almost 
went in by accident.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.890
I-It isn't as though I care what 
happens to some child I don't know.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:13.600
But if I'd pretended I hadn't noticed, 
I wouldn't have slept well. That's all.

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:16.610
<i>Th-This is...</i>

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.690
There's no mistaking it! You're tsundere!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.480
Huh?

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.530
Tsundere?

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:21.530
I'm sorry.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:24.950
That concept doesn't exist 
in this world, does it?

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.570
I feel as though you're poking fun at me.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.450
I have no plans to go in there!

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:31.200
I apologize for worrying you!

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.830
Well, that's fine, then.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:35.210
Now, if you could just do something about that

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.500
"country girl" look on your face...

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.170
But she went in...

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.300
Wait!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.630
"Country girl" face?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.510
I said not to laugh!

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.600
It's the marketplace!

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.070
Are you all right?

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:02.280
Y-Yes, I'm fi—

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:06.320
I-Is something wrong?

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.490
Did you hurt yourself?

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:10.030
N-No...

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.870
It's nothing.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.290
I'm sorry I wasn't looking 
where I was going.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.290
Not at all. I wasn't paying 
proper attention, either.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:18.500
Excuse me for a moment.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:19.250
Huh?

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.130
Huh?

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.590
There you go.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.800
Well, take care, won't you?

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.890
<i>What a kind young lady.</i>

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:35.600
<i>I'm sure she's lovely, 
just the same inside and out.</i>

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:38.060
<i>But those breasts just aren't fair...</i>

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:45.690
<i>Oh, that's right! I haven't 
tried orc meat yet!</i>

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:46.490
<i>Okay.</i>

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.070
<i>I'll ask them to cook it for me at the inn.</i>

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:50.120
Excuse me! I'll take this one.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.200
Coming right up!

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.490
This contains the best part 
of the tenderloin.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.620
But are you going to be able 
to carry it home yourself?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.830
Oh. I'll be fine.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.960
It's so big!

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.300
Here we go.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.920
Well, that's surprising.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.590
You're very strong, miss, 
and you can use storage magic, too?

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.930
Oh, yes. More or less...

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:13.890
There aren't many who can use that magic.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.640
And a child like you can.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.770
Well, that's knocked me for a loop.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.400
I'm only saying this for your own good.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.230
It's dangerous for children around here.
 You should hurry and go home.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:24.320
Huh?

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.110
I'm sorry. I forgot to tell you.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:31.660
Then it's true? Right now, 
here in the capital...

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.570
Yes.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:37.750
Children around our age have been 
disappearing in the last few days.

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.460
Please be careful, miss.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.460
A child that can use magic is valuable.

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:44.590
I will.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:46.510
Wait! A child?

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:47.420
You mean me?

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.100
So children are going missing...

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.600
This must be why things felt odd today, right?

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:56.560
Nano-chan...

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:08.400
You talking to me without thinking was 
outrageously odd as well, Mile-sama.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.450
After all, normal people can't see me.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:15.580
Oh, don't remind me!

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:19.410
But you know, some of it was because 
you talked first, Nano-chan.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:21.790
That's because you're the first person 
in hundreds of years to perceive us,

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.750
the nanomachines, so...

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:25.380
I can't help it.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.960
Fantasy plus nanomachines, huh?

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.800
I guess anything goes...

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:32.720
in alternate worlds.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:36.390
This is a secret just between us.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:39.930
The truth is, "Mile" is 
just an alias I'm using.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.060
I'm really a noble from the 
Kingdom of Brandel named

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:46.770
A
